{
  "id": "repetition-effect",
  "term": "repetition effect",
  "definition": "In this packet, the repetition effect refers to the Hebb repetition effect: improved serial recall when a sequence is repeated across trials. The packet indicates that this memory effect appears across different kinds of visual material and is influenced by whether repeated and filler sequences share the same items.",
